# Nova Notetaker UI Design System

Last updated: 2026-05-26

Purpose: Keep Nova Notetaker visually consistent as it evolves from a prototype into a calm enterprise meeting-intelligence app.

## Product Feel

Nova should feel:

- Calm.
- Reliable.
- Local-first.
- Enterprise-safe.
- Quietly intelligent.
- Focused on meeting outcomes.

Nova should avoid:

- Sci-fi HUD styling.
- Heavy neon.
- Developer-console language.
- Overloaded dashboards.
- Showing infrastructure details unless troubleshooting.

## Themes

Primary theme:

- Executive Dark.

Secondary themes:

- Clean Professional for daytime/accessibility.
- Modern Gradient as a restrained expressive option.

Executive Dark remains the default product identity.

## Color Usage

Orange is the brand accent. Use it sparingly for:

- Primary actions.
- Active navigation.
- Selected tabs.
- Important links.
- Recording/focus accents.
- Dates and review highlights.

Avoid orange on every card border or background. Most surfaces should stay matte charcoal/graphite.

Status colors:

- Success / complete: green.
- Recording / error: red.
- Review / attention: orange.
- Informational / processing: blue.
- Draft / neutral: muted gray.

## Typography

Use simple Segoe UI hierarchy:

- Page title: 24px, bold.
- Panel title: 18px, bold.
- Timer / hero metric: 28px, bold.
- Body text: 13px.
- Section labels: 12px, uppercase, muted.
- Helper text: 12px, muted.

Avoid excessive letter spacing except the Nova brand mark.

## Layout

Main app structure:

- Left sidebar for navigation.
- Center workspace for active work.
- Right rail only when insights are useful.
- Bottom footer for quiet system state.

Recommended spacing:

- Page margins: 28-34px desktop, 16-22px compact.
- Panel padding: 18-22px.
- Card padding: 14-16px.
- Control spacing: 8-14px.

Cards should use 8px radius or less.

## Badges

Meeting status badges should be human-readable:

- Complete.
- Needs review.
- Processing.
- Draft.
- Missing transcript.

Avoid exposing backend strings like `processed_with_warnings` in the main UI.

Insight badges:

- Owner: neutral.
- Due date: orange/date.
- Confidence high: green.
- Confidence medium: amber.
- Confidence low: red.
- State/status: orange or neutral.

## Live Capture

Primary hierarchy:

1. Meeting title.
2. Recording state.
3. Timer.
4. Capture controls.
5. Transcript.
6. Insights.

The user should always understand:

- Whether Nova is recording.
- How long recording or processing has been running.
- Whether mic/system audio are active.
- What Nova has produced so far.

## Meetings

Meetings page should feel like an operational index:

- Sortable.
- Filterable.
- Human-readable statuses.
- Clear open action and review counts.
- Obvious Open meeting action.

This page should avoid feeling like a raw file browser.

## Meeting Overview

The overview should feel like an executive briefing:

1. Executive summary.
2. Action items.
3. Key decisions.
4. Scheduling details.
5. Review needed.
6. Structured notes.
7. Meeting details / health.

Raw transcript and technical health should be available but visually secondary.

## Settings And Templates

Settings should be grouped by concept:

- Device capture.
- Intelligence.
- Transcription.

Most explanatory text should live in tooltips. Show inline helper text only for settings where wrong values are common or costly.

Templates should separate:

- Meeting profiles: context and business purpose.
- Note templates: output structure and writing rules.

## Responsive Rules

Validate important UI changes at:

- 1366x768.
- High DPI / Windows scaling.
- Wide desktop.
- Narrow window.

When space gets tight:

- Hide secondary rails before compressing controls into unreadability.
- Preserve main workflow controls.
- Keep text wrapped instead of adding horizontal scroll.
